    "standardized_narrative": "The Syndicate reported a profit of $355.5m for 2023, significantly up from $16.6m in 2022, with a combined ratio of 83.3%. This strong performance was driven by an excellent underwriting result and robust investment performance. The Syndicate released $89.2m of technical reserves from prior years, primarily from the Casualty, Marine, and Treaty divisions, due to favourable claims development. Gross written premiums increased by 6.0% to $2,110.3m, with significant growth in the Reinsurance portfolio. Notable catastrophe losses in 2023 included Cyclone Gabrielle, Auckland Floods, Hawaii Wildfires, and the Israel/Gaza Conflict. Prior year events like the Russian invasion of Ukraine, Covid-19 pandemic, and Hurricane Ian continued to have ultimate claims estimates.",
